# Normalize all text to LF in the repo (clean for Linux CI and anonymized mirrors).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artifacts (the synthetic example forecasts; the in-repo Full-sample mask;
# the release documentation PDF). Declaring these is not belt-and-braces: with
# `* text=auto` above, a PDF is spared normalization only because Git's sniff
# finds a NUL in the first 8 KB. A rebuild whose leading bytes happen to be
# NUL-free would be CRLF-mangled at check-in, corrupting it with no CI signal.
*.parquet binary
*.npy binary
*.pdf binary
